The code statements that lead to the bug are:
if (UCSI_CCI_CONNECTOR(cci))
    ucsi_connector_change(ucsi, UCSI_CCI_CONNECTOR(cci));
Reason:
The connector number extracted from CCI is used directly as an index into the connector array without checking if it is within the allocated range (1..ucsi->cap.num_connectors), allowing an out-of-bounds access.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (UCSI_CCI_CONNECTOR(cci)) {
    if (UCSI_CCI_CONNECTOR(cci) <= ucsi->cap.num_connectors)
        ucsi_connector_change(ucsi, UCSI_CCI_CONNECTOR(cci));
    else
        dev_err(ucsi->dev, "bogus connector number in CCI: %lu\n",
                UCSI_CCI_CONNECTOR(cci));
}
Reason:
The added bounds check ensures that the connector number is valid (1..num_connectors) before calling ucsi_connector_change(), preventing out-of-bounds array access. Invalid connector numbers are logged as errors and ignored.

